--- body ---
## Context

Title words like `ready`, `done`, `closed`, `open` are status vocabulary in
this system: pseudo-tags consumed by `erg ls` filters, and the lifecycle
states agents reason about. When they appear at the start or end of a title
they read as a status assertion about the ticket itself rather than as a
reference to the command or concept being changed.

Example: ticket 0143 "ready: demote claimed signal from blocker to marker"
parses as "this ticket is ready" before the eye reaches the colon. The
intended reading is "changes to the `erg ready` command."

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg validate` rejects a ticket whose Title (after the leading `Title:`)
      begins or ends with one of: `ready`, `done`, `closed`, `open`
      (case-insensitive, ignoring surrounding punctuation/whitespace).
- [ ] `erg check` surfaces the same rule corpus-wide.
- [ ] Error message points at filename:LINE and names the offending word.
- [ ] Fixture under `src/go/testdata/` covering each forbidden word at start
      and at end, plus one passing case where the word appears mid-title.
- [ ] Decide and document: do existing closed tickets (e.g. 0143, 0144) get
      grandfathered, or do we rewrite their titles? Default: grandfather
      closed tickets, enforce on open + new.
